{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>which HaShem commanded Moses on Mount Sinai</b> — According to our Sages (Torat Kohanim, Behar, parasha 1:1), all the commandments were stated to Moses on Mount Sinai in their general principles, their specific details, and their exact particularizations, and some of them were repeated in the Tent of Meeting. Now the commandments of Leviticus are repetitions. And according to the plain sense, the measure of the verse is: \"which HaShem commanded Moses on Mount Sinai, and on the day He commanded the children of Israel in the wilderness of Sinai to bring their offerings to HaShem\" — for He commanded concerning the consecrations (מִלּוּאִים) on Mount Sinai, and likewise concerning the burnt offering (עֹלָה) and the sin offering (חַטָּאת), and He commanded concerning the meal offering (מִנְחָה), the guilt offering (אָשָׁם), and the sacrifices of the peace offerings (שְׁלָמִים) in the wilderness of Sinai, in the Tent of Meeting. And it is possible that the sense of \"on Mount Sinai\" in this place is: near Mount Sinai, and that is in the Tent of Meeting. And likewise \"the continual burnt offering, which was made on Mount Sinai\" (Numbers 28:6) — for they were not literally on the mountain, for the continual burnt offering was begun only in the Tent of Meeting, as it is written, \"And this is what you shall do upon the altar\" etc. (Exodus 29:38). And likewise \"And they set out from the mountain of HaShem\" (Numbers 10:33), and likewise \"You have dwelt long enough at this mountain\" (Deuteronomy 1:6) — and the reason in all these is that Israel encamped near Mount Sinai, close to it, as it is written (Exodus 19:2), \"And Israel camped there opposite the mountain.\" And there they remained until they journeyed from there to the wilderness of Paran. Now they made the Tent of Meeting and set it up before the mountain, on its east side, and there they began the continual burnt offering. And in the second year they were commanded concerning the standards (דְּגָלִים), and they positioned the Tent in the midst of the camps when they journeyed. Therefore Scripture says here that this is the Torah for the burnt offering and for all the offerings that HaShem commanded on Mount Sinai, on the day He commanded in the wilderness of Sinai — it declares that it was both on Mount Sinai and in the wilderness of Sinai, to inform us that it was not literally on the mountain, in the place of glory where He spoke with him the Ten Commandments, nor in the wilderness of Sinai after they had journeyed from before the mountain, but rather it was in the wilderness of Sinai, before the mountain, within its boundary and close to it, and there was the Tent of Meeting. As He said at the beginning of the matter (Leviticus 1:1), \"And He called to Moses, and HaShem spoke to him from the Tent of Meeting\" — He now informs us of the place of the Tent of Meeting."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:45.843142142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}